From: Diogo Trindade <diogotr7@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: send the stream's POC type to the firmware

The firmware raises a source change when a stream property differs from
what the driver set. HFI_PROP_PIC_ORDER_CNT_TYPE is always set to 0, so
an H.264 stream of another type raises the same change again every time
the bitstream port is restarted. Set the type the firmware reported.

A client that restarts the decoder after its first source change (Steam
Remote Play does) therefore never gets a picture: the stream stays green.
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen2_command.c
@@ -339,7 +339,7 @@
 {
 	struct iris_inst_hfi_gen2 *inst_hfi_gen2 = to_iris_inst_hfi_gen2(inst);
 	u32 port = iris_hfi_gen2_get_port(inst, plane);
-	u32 poc = 0;
+	u32 poc = inst->fw_caps[POC].value;
 
 	inst_hfi_gen2->src_subcr_params.pic_order_cnt = poc;
 
